;; samples/region.aura
;; Provides a deterministic sample region for the checkout pipeline.
;;
;; (api-sample-region) returns a region code that the pricing/tax
;; module knows how to handle. Keeping the sample here (rather than
;; hard-coding in main.aura) lets the region be swapped without
;; touching the entry point.

(define (api-sample-region)
  ;; "US-CA" is exercised by pricing/tax.aura at 8.75% — a non-zero,
  ;; non-trivial rate that produces a clearly different total from
  ;; the tax-free regions (US-OR, US-MT, US-NH) and from the lower
  ;; rate states like US-TX. This makes the diff against the
  ;; reference stdout contract informative.
  "US-CA")
